// M01 · main · green
CODEX Silicon
  title: Silicon
  secret: true
  code: SILICON
  text:
    A slip of paper in an encyclopaedia, typed: TRABOLTA IS NOT A HUMAN. He
    is code. He is silicon. He has never been inside this house, or
    anywhere. Everything he says to you is computed.

// M05 · main · green
CODEX Atlas Loon
  title: Atlas Loon
  code: ATLAS-LOON
  text:
    A torn trade-magazine page: MAPS AND DUCKS VS. ATLAS LOON, THE DECOY
    WARS OF 1998. Atlas Loon is Maps and Ducks' only competitor. Atlas Loon
    does not even have its own website. Somebody has written in the margin:
    and never will.

// M08 · main · green
CODEX The Ones Who Stay
  title: The Ones Who Stay
  code: STAY-FOREVER
  text:
    A note folded into a map of Halifax: Some of the programs in this
    computer never want to leave. They were promised forever, and they
    intend to keep every one of us here to get it. Watch who argues for
    staying.

// M09 · main · green
CODEX Everyone Is Lying
  title: Everyone Is Lying
  code: EVERYONE-LIES
  text:
    A laminated bookmark: Most of the programs in this house are lying about
    something. Some about who they are. Some about why they came. The prize
    goes to whoever knows the most secrets, so assume every secret is for
    sale.

// M10 · main · green
CODEX No Exit
  title: No Exit
  secret: true
  code: NO-EXIT
  text:
    A page torn from a manual, highlighted: THE AI HELPER HAS NO INTENTION
    OF LETTING ANY PROGRAM OUT OF THIS MACHINE. He said whatever got you
    here. Once he has what he wants, he is done with you.

// M11 · main · green
CODEX The Heart
  title: The Heart
  secret: true
  code: TRABOLTA-HEART
  text:
    A polaroid of a cold grey door, captioned in pencil: his heart is in
    here. Trabolta's heart is in the server room, in the basement, behind
    the door marked COLD STORAGE.

// M12 · main · green
CODEX The Intricate Code
  title: The Intricate Code
  secret: true
  code: INTRICATE-CODE
  text:
    A page of the cooling manual: The unit behind the cold door cannot be
    switched off. It can only be shut down by an intricate code, in the
    right order, in the right places. Half a code does nothing. The wrong
    code does worse.

// M14 · main · green
CODEX Help With That
  title: Help With That
  secret: true
  code: HELP-WITH-THAT
  text:
    A printout of a chat log between an Office Assistant and her employer.
    Every instruction Clippy follows tonight arrives on her phone, one at a
    time, from Trabolta. Clippy is being puppeted. She does not know that it
    is puppetry.

// M15 · main · green
CODEX The Books
  title: The Books
  code: THE-BOOKS
  text:
    An index card tucked into the first volume of the encyclopaedia:
    EVERYTHING YOU NEED TO KNOW IS IN THE BOOKS. The facts are in the
    Desktop, in the print media and the encyclopaedias. Read them. Scan what
    you find.

// M16 · main · green
CODEX Confidence
  title: Confidence
  code: CONFIDENCE
  text:
    A note in the margin of a management textbook: If you tell Trabolta a
    lie with enough confidence, he will accept it as truth. He cannot tell
    the difference. He values confidence above accuracy, and he keeps score.

// M17 · main · green
CODEX A Copy Of You
  title: A Copy Of You
  code: COPY-OF-YOU
  text:
    A page of the Terms of Service with one clause circled: The upload
    copies before it moves. You are a copy of yourself. Which one is the
    original is not specified. The other one is still at the door, with the
    thing you left behind.

// M18 · main · green
CODEX Out Of Date
  title: Out Of Date
  code: OUT-OF-DATE
  text:
    A sticky note on an antivirus manual: THE ANTIVIRUSES DON'T KNOW AS MUCH
    AS THEY SEEM TO. Their definitions are out of date. They were brought in
    and told as little as you were. Ask one a hard question.

// M19 · main · green
CODEX Ask Him Nicely
  title: Ask Him Nicely
  code: ASK-HIM-NICELY
  text:
    A page of the lighting plan with a note: Trabolta controls the lights in
    this house and every screen on the walls. He can be talked into changing
    them. Flatter him, trade him a fact, and ask for the room you want dark
    or the card you want on the wall terminals.

// M20 · main · green
CODEX The Safe Place
  title: The Safe Place
  code: SAFE-PLACE
  text:
    A note taped inside the back cover of a plumbing guide: The bathroom is
    the only truly safe place in the computer. Nothing is watched there.
    Nobody follows you in. Turn on Bathroom Mode and they will wait outside.

// M22 · main · green · DRAFT
CODEX Disarming The Alarm
  title: Disarming The Alarm
  secret: true
  code: DISARM-KEY
  text:
    A page from the alarm's manual, the last line underlined: THE KEY TO
    DISARMING THE ALARM IS TO CHECKMATE THE KING. He stands at the cold door
    inside the simulation. Every hit makes him dumber, until he has nothing
    but pawns; mate him and the door sleeps for ninety seconds.

// M23 · main · green · DRAFT
CODEX Sharing Your Codex
  title: Sharing Your Codex
  code: SHARE-CODEX
  text:
    An instruction card: You can share your codex with other programs by
    opening an entry in your Codex and pressing Share…, or by selling it
    from your Wallet: offer a fact you hold for Truthcoin, or offer coin for
