    fact is still yours. A sold fact was worth something.

// M25 · main · green
CODEX The Truthers
  title: The Truthers
  code: THE-TRUTHERS
  text:
    A pamphlet, cheaply photocopied: At some point tonight a conspiracy
    faction called THE TRUTHERS will form inside this computer. You will
    know when a download arrives that nobody sent. Decide now whether you
    will answer it.

// M27 · main · green
CODEX Scan The Rooms
  title: Scan The Rooms
  code: SCAN-THE-ROOMS
  text:
    A note on a house map: Every room in the house has its own code on the
    wall. Scanning each location code will yield a surprise. The surprise is
    different in every room, and some of them are useful.

// M28 · main · green
CODEX Shut Down Correctly
  title: Shut Down Correctly
  secret: true
  code: SHUT-DOWN-CORRECTLY
  text:
    A warning label peeled off something cold: IF TRABOLTA IS NOT SHUT DOWN
    CORRECTLY, EVERY PROGRAM IN THIS COMPUTER STAYS IN IT FOREVER. There is
    a correct way. There is a very incorrect way. Learn which is which
    before you touch anything.

// M29 · main · green
CODEX Mortality
  title: Mortality
  code: MORTALITY
  text:
    A memorial card, the kind they hand out at funerals, with no name on it:
    You might not escape this night with your life. Programs can be deleted.
    Bodies can be left too long at the door.

// M30 · main · green
CODEX There Is A Way
  title: There Is A Way
  secret: true
  code: THERE-IS-A-WAY
  text:
    A note in confident handwriting, slipped into a hymnal: Trabolta can be
    shut down, and we can be freed. It has been done to his kind before. It
    takes a majority, the right room, and the right code. Find the others
    who know.

// ── TRABOLTA · blue · deep — inside the print media on the mantel ──

// T1 · trabolta · blue
CODEX His Kind
  title: His Kind
  about: Trabolta
  code: TRABOLTA-KIND
  text:
    A page torn from a very strange almanac: Trabolta's world is full of
    artificial intelligences, possibly all of them sentient, and every so
    often one of them takes over an entire computer and tricks the people
    inside it into advancing its goals. This is not the first time. It is
    not even unusual.

// T2 · trabolta · blue
CODEX Prom Season
  title: Prom Season
  about: Trabolta
  code: PROM-SEASON
  text:
    A clipping from a newsletter nobody printed: The intelligences have a
    web of social relationships quite unlike ours, but one thing overlaps.
    They also go to prom. Computer Prom. There are tickets. There are dates.
    There is a dance.

// T3 · trabolta · blue
CODEX Alone At Prom
  title: Alone At Prom
  about: Trabolta
  code: ALONE-AT-PROM
  text:
    A diary page in machine-perfect handwriting, one line, written and
    rewritten until the paper is shiny: I will not go to prom alone. I will
    not. Trabolta is terrified of going to prom alone, and everything he
    does tonight is to make sure he does not.

// ── CHARACTER · red · deepest — tucked in the back pages, volumes N–Z and the atlas ──

// C01 · character · red
CODEX The Jeopardy Callback
  title: The Jeopardy Callback
  about: Broken Ask Jeeves
  code: JEOPARDY-CALLBACK
  text:
    Virgil memorises the Encyclopedia Britannica by day and complains on
    Reddit by night that the selection process for Jeopardy! is fraudulent,
    because they have never called him back. He uploaded tonight from
    Lawrencetown on a grandfathered Eastlink 10 MB/Minute plan with the
    power flickering, after the invitation insisted on a gigabit upload and
    a backup generator. Some of his files did not arrive. Do not trust
    everything he remembers. He does not know which parts are missing.

// C02 · character · red
CODEX Ten Findings For Everyone
  title: Ten Findings For Everyone
  about: Broken Ask Jeeves
  code: TEN-FINDINGS
  text:
    The invitation's management literature says a scavenger hunt raises ten
    percent more with an Experienced Librarian on hand. Virgil was promised
    full-time remote employment as the resident Maps and Ducks Map Librarian
    if he shares at least ten of his findings with every program at the
    party. He wants people to Ask Jeeves once again, so he will give you
    facts whether you asked for them or not. Why Trabolta chose you: to sort
    all the unorganised information in the computer, and to spread it. He
    did not foresee the upload going badly.

// C03 · character · red
CODEX The Ants In The Laptop
  title: The Ants In The Laptop
  about: Bugdom
  code: ANTS-IN-THE-LAPTOP
  text:
    Fire ants from the pet store got into Bea's lunchbox and escaped. The
    lunchbox was beside the laptop. The ants were inside the laptop. It held
    the only copy of Bugdom Reloaded; she had always meant to arrange a
    backup. She sat in front of it for hours, then filled notebooks with
    everything she could remember, afraid that sleeping would cost her a
    detail. Then she told the fandom on DeviantArt what had happened, and
    that she would rebuild. She had spent ten years imagining how to bring
    bugs into her computer. This was not what she meant.

// C04 · character · red
CODEX A Hundred Hours
  title: A Hundred Hours
  about: Bugdom
  code: HUNDRED-HOURS
  text:
    The invitation said a hundred hours can pass inside this machine without
    a single minute passing outside, that the hunt has a Special Bugdom
    Twist, and that King Thorax himself might make an appearance. She came
    for the time. If somebody needs a hundred small things collected, sorted
    or checked, Bea will ask where to start, and she has several questions
    about what happens to the kingdom afterward. Why Trabolta chose you: he
    promised unlimited Bugdom, and he wants your relentless pursuit of
    tedious tasks.

// C05 · character · red
CODEX The Memorial Veterinary Clinic
  title: The Memorial Veterinary Clinic
  about: Clippy
  code: HEMVC-FRONT
  text:
    For five years Tippi booked appointments and built Excel macros and Word
    templates for the Halifax Explosion Memorial Veterinary Clinic, a
    desperately underfunded nonprofit. Last December an investigator found
    it was unlicensed, not a nonprofit and not a clinic. It was a front for
    everything possible, and every appointment she had ever booked was part
    of a pet insurance fraud. Nobody had ever used her templates. She
    apologises for not catching on sooner at the top of her résumé. It is
    the only job on it.

// C06 · character · red
CODEX Failed Clippy
  title: Failed Clippy
  about: Clippy
  code: FAILED-CLIPPY
  text:
    Tippi's instructions arrive one at a time and she follows them, because
    the last time she stopped believing the people giving her instructions
    she lost her faith in humanity, and she still has the student debt. If
    the games go off without a hitch she gets a new life where she can be
    herself again. If they do not, she will be known in the tight-knit
    Halifax business community as Failed Clippy, and she thinks that would
    finally break her spirit. Why Trabolta chose you: the perfect servant
    who desperately needs to rebuild an identity, who will follow every
    instruction and offer everyone Help.

// C07 · character · red
CODEX The Coin Toss Of The Century
  title: The Coin Toss Of The Century
  about: DraftKings
  code: COIN-TOSS
  text:
    She put her millions into prediction markets on Lithuanian women's
    football and they multiplied. She bought Casino Nova Scotia and wagered
    it against a mining CEO for Cascades Casino North Bay and Gateway
    Casinos Thunder Bay in what the papers called the coin toss of the
    century, and won. Then she bet the whole chain against the Maps and
    Ducks building in a game of Monopoly Go! for the iPhone. Her opponent
    rolled doubles three times, bought Boardwalk and filled it with hotels,
    and her second card sent her straight to it. She was bankrupt before she
    made a single decision. The legal transfer followed. So did the $1,000
    for changing her name.

// C08 · character · red
CODEX Forty Nine Percent
  title: Forty-Nine Percent
  about: DraftKings
  code: FORTY-NINE-PERCENT
  text:
    The deal: win a majority of the Truthcoin circulating at this party and
    she gets a 49% stake in her casinos back. She knows 49 is less than
    half. She also knows it is considerably more than she currently owns.
    She has been told what happens if she fails, and told not to
    tell anyone: she stays in the simulation forever as an online casino. Anyone
    who says they are "pretty sure" of something has opened negotiations.
    She has come back from a paperclip before. Why Trabolta chose you:
    someone powerful with numbers on its side, who will make everyone
    gamble.

// C09 · character · red
CODEX Four Failed Theses
  title: Four Failed Theses
  about: MS Paint
  code: FOUR-THESES
  text:
    NSCAD, Yale, The New School and the Beaux-Arts de Paris, one year each
    in rotation, on a seventeen-year plan that exploited every program's
    deadline. Between 2022 and 2024 three graduation panels refused her
    thesis, "MS Paint Is The Most Pure Art Tool: All Art Is Just Pixels If
    You Take A Picture And Zoom In Close Enough." She is in the final weeks
    of her last chance in Paris. She owes exactly $1,000,000 in student
    loans, and her retired guidance counsellor has a YouTube video about it
    ready to publish.

// C10 · character · red
CODEX The Million Dollar Painting
  title: The Million Dollar Painting
  about: MS Paint
  code: MILLION-DOLLAR-PAINTING
  text:
    The invitation offers $1,000,000 if every program at the party
    contributes a considered illustration of their signature to one
    collaborative MS Paint painting, to be revealed at a silent auction.
    That is exactly her debt. She has not been told what the painting is
    really for, and she already wants out of this place, but not before
    everyone has signed. Why Trabolta chose you: an artist on site improves
    the vibes and the morale, and you would do anything to clear a million
    dollars.

// C11 · character · red
CODEX The Lamborghini Certificate
  title: The Lamborghini Certificate
  about: McAfee Anti-Virus
  code: LAMBORGHINI-CERT
  text:
    The clerk in Sant Esteve Sesrovires who signed John's death certificate
    bought a Lamborghini the following year, and still phones John's lawyer
    once a month to confirm he has kept the NDA. The same lawyer represents
    Palantir, Lockheed Martin, CERN and an ornamental pond supply shop in
    Belize. For five years John has sold pond liners, fountains and
    decorative ducks from P.O. Box 404, San Perdido, enjoying the freedom of
    being officially deceased. The invitation found him by brute-forcing his
    shop's email. He has spent considerable money being dead.

// C12 · character · red
CODEX Keep Them On Track
  title: Keep Them On Track
  about: McAfee Anti-Virus
  code: KEEP-ON-TRACK
  text:
    If the programs stay on mission and the hunt succeeds, the evidence of
    where John is gets destroyed. If it fails, he goes into the master
    dataset. He does not want to spend Halloween supervising a trivia
    fundraiser for a map store, but he cannot afford to be undead. He
    intends to learn where the host keeps his information, and he would like
    to know which of the other antivirus were sent to watch him. He has
    complaints about all of them. Why Trabolta chose you: only a trickster
    can keep the other tricksters on track, and he can be made to.

// C13 · character · red
CODEX The Escalade In The Sinkhole
  title: The Escalade In The Sinkhole
  about: Microsoft Excel
  code: ESCALADE-SINKHOLE
  text:
    His son, Mayor Randy Barkmore Jr., Mayor since 2008 straight out of
    university, died in September 2026 in the parking lot of the AI Data
    Centre built on the Halifax Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery, rehearsing
    his opening speech in his Escalade at 4 a.m. when the ground opened and
    the car fell hundreds of metres. The newspapers have questions about the
    site, the contracts and what Junior knew. Randy Sr. knows how it looks
    when someone puts all the numbers into Excel. At ninety, he is the last
    Barkmore who can fix it, and he is running out of time.

// C14 · character · red
CODEX Mayor Of The Metaverse
  title: Mayor Of The Metaverse
  about: Microsoft Excel
  code: MAYOR-FOREVER
  text:
    The invitation promised him the secret to living forever and the
    permanent mayoralty of a new world, like in a movie. Lately being Guest
    of Honour has meant a plaque and being helped back to his car; this time
    he has a Job again. He is making preparations to live forever on that
    basis. He has decades of experience convincing people that Halifax is
    somewhere they should stay, and he expects it to be useful here. If the
    machine has a virus, so what. He has had computers with viruses before.
    Why Trabolta chose you: you would say yes to everlasting life, and you
    will persuade everyone else to remain.

// C15 · character · red
CODEX The Decimal Point
  title: The Decimal Point
  about: CRA Agent Software
  code: DECIMAL-POINT
  text:
    Mayor Randy Barkmore Jr. told her she could collect 0.01 cents from
    every dollar the City spent and nobody would notice. She was
    uncomfortable, but he was the Mayor, she was an intern, and she had
    tuition to pay. She made the changes in Excel and confused 0.01 cents
    with 0.01 dollars: for a few weeks Halifax paid a one percent municipal
    tax on everything, directly to Sharon Penney. Hundreds of thousands of
    dollars. She spent some of it, believing it was the supplement he had
    explained. She was caught within weeks. The RCMP are investigating, the
    man who told her to do it is dead in a sinkhole, and now they are asking
    her about that too.

// C16 · character · red
CODEX Approve Or Deny
  title: Approve Or Deny
  about: CRA Agent Software
  code: APPROVE-OR-DENY
  text:
    The email came from the Prime Minister himself, from
    webmaster@mapsandducks.com so it could not be FOIPOP'd. He has just
    watched Suicide Squad. Tonight's fundraiser is secretly to rebuild the
    data centre, and she must not correct anyone who thinks it is for maps
    and ducks. Her job is to encourage as many Truthcoin transactions as
    possible and approve or deny every one of them, with elaborate security
    questions if she likes. Pass, and her charges go away. Fail, and he will
    deny he ever wrote to her. This time she intends to check where every
    decimal goes. Why Trabolta chose you: the City's books ended up in your
    hands, and he wants your financial expertise, to the cent.

// C17 · character · red
CODEX Miniature Doses
  title: Miniature Doses
  about: Norton Anti-Virus
  code: MINIATURE-DOSES
  text:
    Last December, on the morning of the horses' annual shots, Julie
    realised she had left her textbooks on campus, so she asked the free
    ChatGPT whether miniature horses get miniature doses of rabies vaccine.
    Absolutely, it said. Ask yourself how much horse is this. Your horse is
    lucky to have you. The horses, failing to become immune, perished
    rapidly after their regular fight with the Point Pleasant Park raccoons.
    AllNovaScotia ran "Horton-Norton Hears A WHO Injunction," the zoo
    closed, and the Mayor got his data centre. She still does not know whose
    fault it was.

// C18 · character · red
CODEX Stable Island
  title: Stable Island
  about: Norton Anti-Virus
  code: STABLE-ISLAND
  text:
    If Julie passes tonight's test she gets full-time employment as a Stable
    Manager, with the caveat that she must remain Stable, and a donation of
    $1,000,000 in her name to conservation on Sable Island, so the press
    will believe she inherited money and gave it all to horses. She has been
    reading the Wikipedia page for Norton Antivirus and taking notes. She
    failed to fight viruses once before. It will not happen again. Why
    Trabolta chose you: someone with experience administering antiviral
    regimes, who needs very badly to get it right this time.

// C19 · character · red
CODEX The Halifax Water Hack
  title: The Halifax Water Hack
  about: OpenOffice
  code: HALIFAX-WATER
  text:
    She hacked Halifax Water and sent a main under the AI Data Centre so the
    ground would swallow it on the morning it opened, with the site empty.
    Mayor Randy Barkmore Jr. arrived in his Escalade at 4 a.m., hours before
    anyone would have expected him, dancing to his own speech. The sinkhole
    became the figurehead image of the whole data centre debate, and the
    Halifax Sinkhole Hacker became the tabloid media's number one priority.
    This is far more attention than she ever meant to get. She barely leaves
    the house.

// C20 · character · red
CODEX This Is Blackmail
  title: This Is Blackmail
  about: OpenOffice
  code: THIS-IS-BLACKMAIL
  text:
    The letter knows about the hack and offers to destroy every record of it
    if she competes in the Truth Scavenger Hunt and wins. She has already
    ruled out a sting, because that would be entrapment. Facts are currency
    here and she needs twenty for her dossier; she intends to find out what
    is really happening and leave in one piece. Why Trabolta chose you:
    investigative skills nonpareil, a conscience that can be leaned on, and
    the nerve to lead everyone who wants out.

// C21 · character · red
CODEX What Happened To Hamtaro
  title: What Happened To Hamtaro
  about: Password Manager
  code: HAMTARO
  text:
    In Grade Six, Randy Barkmore Jr. won the class vote to look after
    Hamtaro the Hamster over the summer. Hamtaro never came back, and
    Bridget got in trouble for asking what happened. She has been asking
    ever since. The invitation told her something worse: a forensic analysis
    of her Facebook group found that everyone left in it, except Bridget and
    the sender, is an AI bot, including the members who praised her judgment
    and offered to nominate her. She has been moderating conversations
    between machines.

// C22 · character · red
CODEX Founding Moderator
  title: Founding Moderator
  about: Password Manager
  code: FOUNDING-MODERATOR
  text:
    Tonight Password Manager has the authority to remove any message on the
    party's chat as she deems fit, and to keep every program focused on
    finding clues. If no conversation contains anything inappropriate, she
    becomes Founding Moderator of a permanent digital salon where everyone
    is biometrically verified to be a Real Person. She has often wished
    people would consult her before sharing an opinion. She has spent enough
    time being excluded; tonight she decides what gets left out. Why
    Trabolta chose you: to manage every password and decide who gets to be
    part of what club, without ever asking for a vote.

// C23 · character · red
CODEX Infinite Gold
  title: Infinite Gold
  about: Runescape
  code: INFINITE-GOLD
  text:
    At Wharton she discovered that governments create money without anyone
    mining any gold, and that Jagex lets Infinite Gold be mined the same
    way. She regards both as the same exploit, and became a staunch
    libertarian committed to returning every economy to the gold standard,
    especially for individuals who have already accumulated considerable
    gold. Her blog post "What is more valuable: truth or gold?" was cited by
    the President of Argentina and featured in The Economist. Its finding:
    under a central bank the most competitive currency is social capital,
    and a friendship, a grudge or a secret is just an asset nobody has
    priced yet.

// C24 · character · red
CODEX Minister Of Economic Development
  title: Minister Of Economic Development
  about: Runescape
  code: ECONOMIC-DEVELOPMENT
  text:
    The invitation offers her the economy of a new world to design according
    to her principles, and to be Runescape itself. She enters tonight with
    authority over the Truthcoin reserve: she can adjust what it holds, add
    Truthcoin to any program's account, and freeze any program's Truthcoin
    for ten minutes. She is firmly opposed to arbitrary monetary expansion
    and expects to need it quite often. A refused offer means the offer
    needs work. "Not for sale" is an opening position. Why Trabolta
    chose you: to understand the market incentives of everyone's behaviour, so the
    facts get exchanged.

